      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BELVEDERE MISS (5) collected her maiden over today's journey at Mackay two runs ago. Stepped up to 1300m in a BM58 here last start and did well to be beaten under two lengths after being in the firing line all the way. This looks an ideal set-up. LUXOR PRINCE (6) has not won since May 2022 but produced a real eye-catcher here last time out, flashing home for third at the end of 1400m. Coming back in trip is a small concern, as is the win drought. Each-way prospects. BOLD AS BRASS (1) was too bad to be true over 1100m at Gatton last start, that run following a good second over today's trip at Kilcoy ten days earlier. Draws a nice gate and should be given another chance. SPITZBERG (9) backs up six days after making late ground to be beaten just 1.4 lengths over 1100m at Mackay. Better placed over this trip. MAKING HISTORY (10) has been hitting the line well in shorter races and will appreciate getting over more ground this time.",
